The AAR published by this project bundles FFmpeg libraries (libavcodec,
libavutil and libswresample) linked into libffmpegJNI. FFmpeg is Copyright (c)
2000-2026 the FFmpeg developers and is licensed under the GNU Lesser General
Public License, version 2.1 or later. FFmpeg's own license file ships in the
AAR as META-INF/media3-ffmpeg-decoder/FFMPEG-LICENSE.md. FFmpeg is built without
--enable-gpl, --enable-nonfree and --enable-version3.

Changes put.io made to FFmpeg (LGPL 2.1 section 2a):

- 2026-11-08: libavcodec/ac3dsp.c and libavcodec/aarch64/Makefile are changed by
  patches/ffmpeg-lgpl-only.patch, so the ac3 and eac3 decoders use the C
  implementation on arm64. Both files carry a dated notice of the change.
- 2026-11-08: libavcodec/aarch64/ac3dsp_init_aarch64.c and
  libavcodec/aarch64/ac3dsp_neon.S are deleted. FFmpeg licenses them under the
  GPL and builds them without --enable-gpl.
- Every other file in the FFmpeg tree whose header grants the GPL is deleted
  too. None of them is compiled into this project.

Source and build instructions for FFmpeg in a released AAR:

- Every release publishes the corresponding source next to the AAR on Maven
  Central, signed like the AAR. It has the classifier ffmpeg-source:
  https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/io/put/media3-ffmpeg-decoder/<version>/media3-ffmpeg-decoder-<version>-ffmpeg-source.tar.xz
- That archive holds the FFmpeg source that was built, the patch, the JNI
  wrapper that links it, the build scripts, and BUILD.txt with the commands to
  rebuild FFmpeg and relink libffmpegJNI.so.
- Every AAR carries META-INF/media3-ffmpeg-decoder/ffmpeg-build.txt with the
  exact FFmpeg commit, build script and per-ABI configure lines, and the LGPL
  text in META-INF/media3-ffmpeg-decoder/COPYING.LGPLv2.1.

